@HUMAN
Press P to pause the game. You may issue orders while the game is paused. Press P again to resume the game.
~
Press K to quickly find and select your King.
~
If you choose the Small Buildings option, you will have more open space for building, maneuver and battle.
~
Generals who have troops to command will steadily increase their leadership skills. The more troops the better.  These troops will also help to keep up a General's loyalty level.
If a General has no troops to command, his leadership levels will stagnate and his loyalty will fall.
~
The leadership level of your commanders greatly influences the ability of your troops.  Leaders with high levels of leadership will train their soldiers faster and will give them more power in combat.
~
Beginning players should try playing the game at Difficulty Level I.  Once you have mastered this level, go on to more difficult levels.
~
Every Seat of Power gives a unique benefit to its civilization.  You should be aware of these benefits as you plan your long range strategy.
Press D to quickly find and select your Seat of Power.
~
Your population will grow faster if your people have jobs and a steady supply of goods in their markets.
~
Enemy soldiers with the high levels of loyalty will be the most difficult to bribe, while those with low levels of loyalty will be the easiest.
The larger the bribe offer, the more likely that it will be accepted.
~
Skilled leaders and spies may be hired from inns.  If you build several inns, you will have a wider selection of these mercenaries.
Press I to quickly find and select one of your inns.  Continue pressing I to cycle through all of your inns.
~
Powerful artifacts are often available for purchase at inns.  Click on the mercenary who is carrying one and then Click on the artifact to purchase it.
~
To complete your research projects more quickly, build more towers of science.
Press T to quickly find and select one of your towers of science.
~
To help catch enemy spies, place your own spies in your towns and forts.  You may have to research Counter Espionage before these spies can be effective, however.
~
Building walls around your towns will help to protect your townspeople from attack.  Your townspeople cannot be injured as long as the walls still stand.
~
Right-Click on the repair hammer to automatically repair all of your buildings.  Right-Click again to turn off automatic repair.
~
Attacking some units from behind or from the side can be more effective than attacking them from the front.
~
Some units are stronger in hand-to-hand fighting than others.
Make sure that you put these units in front of units that specialize in range attack.
~
Your civilians can not go to work in a building unless there is a linking line from the building to their town.
~
Your leaders cannot assert their control over a town unless they are in a fort or camp that is linked to the town.
Towns may rebel against your rule if you fail to exert your control over them for too long of a period.
~
Your reputation will affect the loyalty of your people and your ability to influence others.  To keep a high reputation, don't break treaties and don't slaughter civilians.
~
For a wider view of the world, play in 1024X768 resolution.  This will, of course, work better with faster computers.
~
Caravans are sacrosanct.  You cannot attack them!
~
Your soldiers will increase their skills over time, so don't waste valuable veterans and expect to replace them quickly.
~
Use Alt + Right-Click to set Waypoints for selected units or for entire troops of soldiers.
~
Set Rally Points for units produced in War Factories or Special Structures by Right-Clicking anywhere on the ground or on forts or camps.
The War Factory or the Special Structure must be selected when you do this.
When the unit has been trained or the weapon built, it will go to that rally point.
~
Reply "Accept" to certain diplomatic messages by Right-Clicking on the color square.  If you wish to see further options, Click on the color square.
~
The money that you make from selling imported goods is greater than the cost of importing them.
So if you have no goods of your own, you can still make money on imports.
Just be sure to have enough money on hand before your caravan reaches a foreign market because you will have to pay for what you pick up.
~
You may pick up goods from foreign markets, but you may not drop them off.
~
If another kingdom wants your goods they will send caravans to your markets to pick them up.
~
Increase the number of spaces open for workers in a building by sliding the counter to the right.
Decrease the number of space by sliding the counter to the left.
~
You may attempt to attack Greater Beings if you wish, but you cannot harm them!  They will only disappear when their Prayer Points have been exhausted.
~
Some of your soldiers will increase their leadership and combat levels faster than others.  Keep these units in mind as you search for new commanders.
~
To help lower the resistance of independent towns, place a General of the same nationality in a linked fort or camp.
The higher his leadership, the more the resistance will fall.
Giving these independent people jobs will further lower their resistance, although they won't accept jobs until their resistance has fallen below 50.
~
If you can pick up the Scroll of Power of another nationality, you will have the opportunity of building another Seat of Power and accessing its benefits.
You will need a town of the appropriate nationality, linked to the new Seat of Power, to supply people to pray for the new Greater Being.
~
Your towns will reach capacity once they have 100 citizens.  In order to continue increasing your population, you should settle new towns.
~
You may rename your towns by Right-Clicking on the town name above the town interface.  Then type in the new name and Click OK.
~
The best way to move a large number of civilians over long distances is by wagons.  When a town is selected, Click on the Wagon Icon.
This will fill a wagon with up to 10 civilians.  Send them into other towns of the same nationality or use the wagon to build a new town.
~
Help to protect your forts by arming your towers.
Do this by selecting your fort and Clicking up to five times on the number button above the Towers Icon.
~
To keep a steady flow of tax money into your coffers, set an Auto-Tax for your towns.
To do this, select a town and then Right-Click on the Tax Icon.
Then Right-Click on one of the numbers.  When the loyalty level of a town reaches this number, it will be taxed.
~
When you fight Fryhtans your reputation level will increase at a faster rate than normal.
Powerful heroes will also be more likely to join the forces of those kingdoms that are known as Fryhtan fighters.
~
You can see a wide range of options under the Options Menu.  To get there, Click on the Menu Button and then on Options.
~
Press F6, Click on the Tech Button, or select any of your towers of science to quickly check the status of your current research project.
~
Your games will automatically be saved every two months (of game time).
If you have made a serious blunder and wish to correct it, load one of the two auto-saved games and try again!
~
If you are thinking of purchasing the throne of another kingdom, remember that, if successful, you will inherit that kingdom's problems as well!
~
Your greatest resource is people and at the beginning of the game most of the world's people reside in independent towns.
Your strategy should be obvious; get as many of these towns under your thumb as soon as you can.
~
The upkeep cost for war machines can be quite expensive.  Be careful that you do not build more weapons than you can afford!
~
Your troops can only increase their skills in battle, or in their forts.  Because of this, it is wise not to keep them standing around outside with nothing to do.
If you do, not only will their skills not increase, but their loyalty will steadily fall.
~
Click on AUTO in your factories to insure that they will be producing finished goods from whatever raw materials are available in linked markets or mines.
~
@FRYHTAN
Press P to pause the game.  You may issue orders while the game is paused.  Press P again to resume the game.
~
Press K to quickly find and select your All High Fryhtan.
~
Fryhtan Ordos who have crouls to command will steadily increase their leadership skills.  The more crouls the better.
These crouls will also help to keep up an Ordo's loyalty level.  If an Ordo has no crouls to command, his leadership levels will stagnate and his loyalty will fall.
~
If you choose the Small Buildings option, you will have more open space for building, maneuver and battle.
~
The leadership level of your commanders greatly influences the ability of your troops.
Leaders with high levels of leadership will train their crouls faster and will give them more power in combat.
~
Beginning players should try playing the game at Difficulty Level I.  Once you have mastered this level, go on to more difficult levels.
~
Make sure that you build new Fryhtan lairs within linking distance of as many independent human towns or independent Fryhtan lairs as possible.
This will enable you to enslave those towns once you have beaten down their resistance and to purchase the loyalty of those independent Fryhtan lairs.
~
A good way to get Life Points and to damage your human enemies is to attack their towns.
By culling their population centers you can severely limit their ability to expand.
~
If a human civilian ever surrenders to your forces, you should put him to work building an inn or two.
You will then have the opportunity of purchasing human spies and soldiers or powerful artifacts.
~
Right-Click on the repair hammer to automatically repair all of your buildings.  Right-Click again to turn off automatic repair.(Attacking some units from behind or from the side can be more effective than attacking them from the front.(Some units are stronger in hand-to-hand fighting than others.  Make sure that you put these units in front of units that specialize in range attack.
~
For a wider view of the world, play in 1024X768 resolution.  This will, of course, work better with faster computers.
~
Caravans are sacrosanct.  You cannot attack them!
~
Your Ordos and Crouls will increase their skills over time, so don't waste valuable veterans and expect to replace them quickly.
~
Use Alt + Right-Click to set Waypoints for selected troops.
~
Set Rally Points for units produced in Fryhtan Special Structures by Right-Clicking anywhere on the ground or on lairs.
The Special Structure must be selected when you do this.
~
Reply "Accept" to certain diplomatic messages by Right-Clicking on the color square.  If you wish to see further options, Click on the color square.
~
You will cease to collect tribute from slave towns if you no longer have an Ordo or the All High in a linked lair.
If you wish to continue receiving tribute, make sure to appoint a commander to the lair when your troop leaves to do battle.
~
Some of your Crouls will increase their leadership and combat levels faster than others.  Keep these units in mind as you search for new commanders.
~
You will almost certainly run out of money unless you enslave human towns.
Try to enslave at least one as soon as you are able and remember that you will be unable to extort money from your slaves if you have no commander in the lair that is linked to the slave town.
~
You can see a wide range of options under the Options Menu.  To get there, Click on the Menu Button and then on Options.
~
Your games will automatically be saved every two months (of game time).
If you have made a serious blunder and wish to correct it, just load one of the two auto-saved games!
~
Your troops can only increase their skills in battle, or in their lairs.  Because of this, it is wise not to keep them standing around outside with nothing to do.
If you do, not only will their skills not increase, but their loyalty will steadily fall.
~
@CAMPAIGN
If you have an extremely valuable soldier and you wish to use him in later missions, Click on the R button in the selected soldier's interface.
To find and cycle through your Royal units, press the R key on your keyboard.
~
Press F8 to remind yourself of the goals for your current mission.
~
